proposed_areas.fix_scope:
Run L4, after l4-cred-engine merges (it shares compose.ts, agent.ts, credential-wait.ts and result.ts under the shared-files rules in l4-cred-engine's fix_scope; re-find every line on that head). One commit per item, in this order: L4-creds-15, L4-creds-16, L4-creds-17, L4-creds-18, L4-creds-19, L4-creds-20, L4-creds-21, L4-creds-22, L4-creds-23, L4-creds-24, L4-creds-25, L4-creds-26, L4-creds-27, L4-creds-28, L4-creds-29. Each item starts with its failing test at the person's boundary:
- a UI test in apps/ui/test that clicks the control and asserts what appears and what goes over the wire;
- a real-daemon case for every new or changed route, in its own describe block 'l4-cred-screens, run L4' appended to apps/ui/test/real-daemon.test.ts, with apps/ui/test/fake-daemon.ts and its fixtures changed in the same commit (GET /projects/:id/start-check's credential field, GET /inbox's ask and plan cards, GET /projects/:id/tasks and /status, GET /running, POST /chat with heldTurn, GET /me, POST /sessions, the costs route, POST /projects/:id/pull-requests/:n/merge);
- an exact-string unit test for every sentence, with design section 5's lengths;
- exact-text assertions for model-facing text (L4-creds-27: the project_create definition and the chat system prompt as chatCalls[0] receives them);
- composed twice on one home for every stored mark (the kept start at the month's start, the wait's need, the zone after it is saved).
Then the siblings (validation rule 8): every screen that names a credential, its wait or its figure (Settings, the Start dialog, the plan card, New task's runs-on line, the Tasks row and drawer, the Overview, Home, the session page, the run indicator, chat, Costs), and every '(s)' plural and 'CHF 0.00' for an amount above zero in packages/runtime/src.
Do not touch:
- the engine's reading of stops, notifications and chat's failure, hold and start words (l4-cred-engine);
- the run indicator's states (l4-cred-engine owns run-indicator.ts this round);
- the over-budget lines of the Start dialog (d1109-oversize-*);
- the sessions list's other words (d1109-sessions);
- chat's recall and depth (the chat group).
Shared files: compose.ts (this area: the ask closure :1790-1830, keepStart :4291-4330 and onGrant :5081-5115 on top of l4-cred-engine's idempotence guard); agent.ts (this area: the chat.human write and the held turn); credential-wait.ts (this area: the needs field and waitThenStartSentence); result.ts (this area: the wait result's money clause); transcript.ts (this area: only the skip of hold replies in historyMessages); SessionPage.tsx and SessionsTab.tsx (this area: the time formatting calls and the allowance link). The three items from other subsystems (L4-creds-22 merge, L4-creds-23 onerepo fake daemon, L4-creds-27 project.create description) move to the area the session lead names, with their files.
Security: never weaken the hooks or the sandbox. No credential value, fingerprint, source id or provider text on any screen. Text from pages, searches, files, cards, chat history, reports or any record never becomes instructions to a model. The held turn's model history drops only the app's own hold reply. The merge PUT stays pinned to the sha.
Money: no budget, wrap-up line, monthly cap or plan-share cap is ever passed. 'Use API key' never raises a budget, and the widening yes is always the person's tap. The figure is capped by the work budget. The yes runs only the work its figure counts.
Docs: a dated amendment to ADR 0120 (the one figure; what the yes lets in; the needs row), docs/maintainers/apps.md (the Start dialog, the plan card, Costs, the time helpers), runtime.md (start-check's waitingWorkUsdMicro; heldTurn), commands.md (project.create's description), docs/user-guide.md (When Claude runs out; times in your zone), and the U-entries' Check in the app steps. Do not edit CHANGELOG.md, docs/status/UPDATE-LOG.md or docs/requirements.md.
Before reporting: a bench walk before (from a worktree branch at the base) and after, on --provider bench-api with the subscription stand-in at its limit under ask (LC-C24's figures), a refused key (LC-C21), key_then_subscription with the key limited (LC-C26's dialog), and a person zone different from the browser's (LC-C26's session page). Then pnpm check, pnpm test:integration, pnpm test:e2e, the UI suite and Playwright, run under flock /tmp/frbench/heavy.lock.
